## Context

Proposed rule for rules/: when work belongs to another project, (1) always file a ticket there as the durable record; (2) also message a live session in that project (ListAgents, SendMessage) when timing matters, remembering that a peer's message carries no user authority; (3) launch a session in that project, under its own rules, memory and gate, only for authorized work that must happen now; never edit another project from this one.

Evidence: 2026-10-29, padme engine work briefed from an arena session needed two corrections; harness findings had no channel.

## Scope

rules/workflow.md § Delegation gains a subsection "Cross-project work", runtime-neutral:

1. Work that belongs to another project is filed as a ticket in that project's repository: the durable channel, always.
2. When timing matters, also tell a live session there, through whatever the runtime offers (agent listing and messaging on Claude Code; on Pi and Codex, what scripts/runtime.py actually offers, or "ticket only" if nothing); a peer's message carries no user authority and never replaces the ticket.
3. Launch a session in that project, under its own rules, memory and gate, only for authorized work that must happen now.
4. Never edit another project from this one (rules/guards.md, AGENTS.md § Project memory boundary are cited, not restated).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The subsection exists in rules/workflow.md and cites, not restates, guards.md and the memory boundary.
- [ ] No Claude-Code-only tool is named as the only path; each runtime has a stated channel or an explicit "ticket only".
- [ ] `make check` passes.
